      "content": "WTHR NAM0 colour bytes are RGB, not BGRA: byte0 = R, byte1 = G, byte2 = B, byte3 = reserved. Authority: xEdit wbByteColors = Red(u8), Green(u8), Blue(u8), wbUnused(1) (Core/wbDefinitionsCommon.pas:6962). Measured: the 4th byte is 0 in all 1,480 values of the 37-record corpus, so it is padding and not alpha. The landed helper engine/sky_weather_system.h:750-757 bgraToRgb has a WRONG name and comment (\"ESM colours are packed BGRA (0xAARRGGBB)\") but already decodes byte0->R, byte1->G, byte2->B correctly, so the packed value is really 0x00BBGGRR. Renaming it is fine; swapping its body to match the old name would turn the sky orange. Verify by reading Clear's Sun field: Day must be (255,183,85) orange-yellow, and BGRA gives (85,183,255) sky-blue which is wrong for a sun.",
