      "content": "Oblivion ESM/ESP binary format confirmed: 20-byte record header (NOT the 16-byte header used by Skyrim/Fallout). Record = tag(4) + dataSize(4) + flags(4) + formID(4) + version(2) + unknown(2) = 20 bytes. GRUP = 'GRUP'(4) + size(4) + label(4) + groupType(4) + skip(4) = 20 bytes. Subrecord = tag(4) + size(2) = 6 bytes, with size masked by (size & 0xFFFF). TES4 header record sits at offset 0 with dataSize=744, flags=1, formID=0, so the first GRUP is at offset 764 (20 + 744). app/src/main/cpp/assets/esm_reader.cpp already implements this format correctly (L116 'TES4 record: 20-byte header', L183 'remaining 16 bytes', L86 'GRUP header (20 bytes)', L471 size & 0xFFFF + offset += 6). CRITICAL: records with size 0 are LEGAL and are NOT terminators; treating them as errors truncates the scan.",
