      "content": "Batch 2026-10-19 (session 9427ac74): bsa103-hash-identify RESOLVED - BSA v103 u64 hash algorithm fully recovered from Oblivion.exe. hash32 (EXE 0x6FA040): h = h*0x1003F + tolower(c) mod 2^32. build (EXE 0x6FA080): lo32 sig = [last, penult (0 if len<=2), len, first] bytes; hi32 = (len>3 ? hash32(name+1, (len-3)&0xFF) : 0) + (extra ? hash32(extra) : 0); extension tweak table 0xB25374 ['', '.NIF', '.KF', '.DDS', '.WAV'] case-insensitive, index k adds out[3]+=(k&0xFC)<<5, out[0]+=(k&0xFE)<<6, out[1]+=(k<<7)&0xFF. folder_hash = build(name, NULL) (trailing backslash stripped, empty -> '.'); file_hash = _splitpath -> build(fname, ext). Query: 0x42E85A strips leading backslash and Data-prefix -> 0x6FA1B0 split -> 0x6FA2D0 modes 0=file/1=folder/2=raw -> lookup 0x42CE40 / 0x42D000 (u64 two-dword binary search, cmp fn 0x42BC10). Verified 100%: folders 1621/1621, files 147629/147629 across all 17 Steam BSAs. Prior murmur2_64/FNV1a64 8-variant attempts failed (algorithm is custom multiply-add). Docs: tmp/re/s76_file_hash_analysis.md, tmp/re/s76_hash_verify.py; s76_bsa_v104.md issues 1/4 marked RESOLVED."
