      "content": "Oblivion MGEF/SPEL/ENCH/INGR/ALCH binary layout (empirically confirmed with Python probes mgef_probe7..12 against the real Oblivion.esm). MGEF subrecord is DATA (36 or 64 bytes; NOT MEDT): off4=baseCost(float), off8=actorValue(uint32), off12=school(0-5), off16=flags. SPEL subrecord SPIT is 16 bytes: off0=spellType, off4=cost, off8=level, off12=uninitialized (0xCDCDCD00; NOT flags). EFID (4 bytes) is the MGEF editorID ASCII code (e.g. FIDG, RESP, INVI), NOT a formID. EFIT is 24 bytes: off0-3 = EFID echo, off4=magnitude, off8=area, off12=duration, off16=unused, off20=actorValue. The old code read magnitude/area/duration from off0/off4/off8, i.e. 4 bytes off; that was the direct cause of 0 spells being assigned. INGR/ALCH: DATA is only 4 bytes (float weight) and ENIT is 8 bytes (off0=value, off4=flags).",
