      "content": "Phase 69 (Persistence) implemented by Copilot session 9427ac74. save_format_version.h CURRENT_VERSION raised to 4 (v3 = SCRP script globals, v4 = CNTR containers). save_manager.cpp now serializes/restores QSTS (completed quests), SCRP (ScriptManager globals via oblivion::script::ScriptValue) and CNTR (container lock flag + InventorySlot list). Namespacing gotcha: ScriptValue/ScriptManager live in namespace oblivion::script; save_manager.cpp is at global scope so full qualification is mandatory (build error 'unknown type name ScriptValue' at save_manager.cpp L271/667/668). WorldManager gained a container registry (registerContainer/unregisterContainer/getAllContainers/getContainerByFormID) backed by containers_ keyed on FormID; registerContainer rejects FormID 0. Container gained formID/getFormID/setFormID/clearItems(); populateFromESM(esm, baseFormID) builds the inventory from the CONT record and sets formID. Renderer::activateNearestContainer(maxDistance, message) materialises the nearest CONTAINER REFR (refType==0) in the current cell on first use, registers it with WorldManager, and opens UIContainerMenu; identity uses the REFR FormID (best->formID) because it is unique per placement. Containers present in a save but not yet materialised are buffered in SaveManager::pendingContainers_ (std::unordered_map<uint32_t, PendingContainerState>) and applied by SaveManager::applyPendingContainerState(container) on first open; saveGame() also carries forward still-buffered containers so an unopened container is not dropped by a save/load round trip. Virtual controller X button order is now door -> container -> pickup; anyMenuOpen() includes containerMenuUI so world input is blocked while the container menu is visible. Still open: REF change state (needs .ess analysis, docs/RE_EXE_REPORT.md), and on-device save/load round-trip verification of container contents.",
