      "content": "Phase 69 container persistence is now covered by the host test suite (2026-10-22, Copilot session 9427ac74). New app/src/main/cpp/tests/phase69_persistence_tests.cpp/.h -> class Phase69PersistenceTests (30 assertions on a green run), wired into tools/host_tests/host_runner_main.cpp. It uses save slots 90/91 (kSlotA/kSlotB) so a developer's real saves are never touched, and removeSlot() cleans them up at the start and end. Four cases: (1) materialised round trip - chest with two items and locked=true through saveGame -> loadGame -> applyPendingContainerState; (2) empty container still writes and reloads as empty and unlocked; (3) carry-forward - a save taken while the container was never materialised must keep the buffered pendingContainers_ entry; (4) the pending buffer is consumed by the first applyPendingContainerState() and an unknown FormID returns false. IMPORTANT ROOT CAUSE FOUND: the Phase 69 commit (957319e8) had silently broken the host suite. save_manager.cpp calls Container::addItem/clearItems/setLocked, but game/container.cpp and game/interactable.cpp were absent from tools/host_tests/run_host_tests.sh SOURCES, so the single g++ invocation failed with 'ld.exe: save_manager.cpp: undefined reference to Container::addItem(InventorySlot const&)'. MinGW/PE resolves every symbol in every translation unit and --gc-sections cannot remove undefined references, so a stale SOURCES list fails the link rather than a test. Fix: added game/container.cpp, game/interactable.cpp and tests/phase69_persistence_tests.cpp to SOURCES (now 83 translation units, was 80). Also corrected the stale '.github/workflows/android.yml' comment from '53 translation units' to 83 and documented the new suite plus the mid-layer dependency rule in tools/host_tests/README.md. Rule to remember: a leaf header may be stubbed, but any mid-layer .cpp whose symbols a wired suite (or a manager in SOURCES) reaches must be listed for real.",
